hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3301","Ubayd Allah ibn Abdul Karim informed me, he said: Abdul Rahman ibn Abdul Malik told me, he said: Ibn Abi Fudaik told me, on the authority of Musa Bin Yaqoub, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, that Muhammad bin Muslim al-Zuhri informed him that Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik Al-Ansari, and Amr bin Abdullah bin Unais Al-Juhani told him that Abdullah bin Unais told them that a group of Ansar, They said: Who is the man who asks the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Abdullah said: So I said: I am. They said: Go and ask him for us when is the Night of Decree? So I went out until I found the sunset at some verses of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and prayed. Maghrib prayer, and when he finished praying, I went out with him until he entered his house and I was with him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him to break his fast. When he finished The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for his shoes, then said: “I think you have a need.” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God, he has sent me to you. So-and-so and so-and-so ask you when is Laylat al-Qadr? That is the night of the twenty-second of Ramadan, so I said: Tonight is the night of the twenty-second of Ramadan? He said: “Rather, the Qibla on the night of the twenty-third.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Musa bin Yaqoub is not that strong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3302","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told me, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Uyaynah, he is Ibn Abdul-Rahman, told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Abu Bakra said: I did not seek it except in the last ten nights after something I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I heard him say “Seek it in the last ten days of the nine or seven days that remain,” and he also mentioned the five days, saying: “Or the last three or three nights.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3303","Humayd ibn Masada narrated on the authority of Yazid, who was the son of Zuray’, who said: Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I mentioned Laylat al-Qadr with Abu Bakra, and he said: I am not seeking it after something I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except in The last ten nights, for I heard him say: “Seek it in the last seven nights, or in the last five nights, or in the last three nights,” and it was Abu Tomorrow he will pray on the twentieth of Ramadan like he prays during the rest of the year. When the tenth day begins, he will strive"
"3304","Amr bin Zurarah narrated, he said: Ismail narrated, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, secluded himself during the middle ten days of Ramadan, seeking Laylat al-Qadr before it was revealed to him. When they had passed, He ordered the building to be built, and it was annulled. Then it was made clear that it would happen during the last ten nights. So he ordered the building to be done, and it was repeated. He secluded himself for the last ten nights and revolted against the people. He said: “I was informed of the Night of Decree, so I came out to tell you about it. Then two men came with them, the devil, and I forgot about it, so they sought it at nine o’clock.” And on the seventh and on the fifth.”"
"3305","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdah, he heard Zurra saying: I asked Ubayyah, I said: Your brother is Ibn Masoud. He says: Whoever spends the year in prayer will receive Laylat al-Qadr. He, may God have mercy on him, said: It is known that in the month of Ramadan it is the twenty-seventh night, then He swears, making no exception, “It is the night of the twenty-seventh.” I said: What do you say that about, O Abu Al-Mundhir? He said: “By the sign that was foretold by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that it will appear on that day without a ray.” Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported something similar on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr. Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Zirr, and the like."
"3306","Muhammad ibn al-Ala reported, he said: Ibn Dris told us, he said: I heard Ismail, he said: I saw a button in the mosque whose beard was filled with pride, I asked him: How old have you reached? He said: One hundred and twenty years, and he said: I heard my father saying: “Laylat al-Qadr is the twenty-seventh night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3307","Muhammad Ibn Al-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, he said: Al-Ajlah told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Zirr Ibn Hubaysh, he said: I heard Ubaya, he says: “I know that it is the night of the twenty-seventh, which is the night that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, foretold about its day.” And its night appears white in the morning as if it were a basin with no beams.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Ajlah is not that strong, and he was He has a bad opinion (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3308","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that he heard Abu Hudhayfah talking, on the authority of A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I looked at the moon on the Night of Destiny and saw it as if it had split a veil,” Abu Ishaq said. : That would only be the morning of the twenty-third. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3309","Muhammad ibn Ali reported, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told us, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs the Night of Decree out of faith and seeking reward, God will forgive him for his previous sins.” \His sin\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"3310","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abd. The Most Gracious, he said: Abu Hurairah told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever observes Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his sins will be forgiven. \"" 3311"""""
"3311","'Abd al-Hamid ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, saying: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward (ihtisab), his previous sins will be forgiven, and whoever stands (in prayer) on the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr) out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."""""
"3312","Amr bin Uthman reported, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Abu Amr, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward from Him, his previous sins will be forgiven, and whoever stands in Laylat al-Qadr out of faith And out of hope, he will be forgiven for his previous sins.”"
"3313","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa narrated, he said: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Al-Awza’i narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays the month of Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, all his previous sins will be forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3314","Abu Dawud told me, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Salamah told him, Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever observes Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, all his previous sins will be forgiven.”"
"3315","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.”"
"3316","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Whoever fasts the month of Ramadan out of faith and in the hope of seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven, and whoever stands in Laylat al-Qadr out of faith and in the hope of seeking reward.” He will be forgiven for his previous sins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3317","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever stands in Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven, and whoever stands for Laylat Al-Qadr with faith And out of hope, he will be forgiven for his previous sins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3318","Muhammad bin Khalid reported, saying: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abd informed me. The Most Gracious, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say about Ramadan: “Whoever rises in it out of faith and in the hope of seeking reward, will be forgiven for what he does.” He came forward from his sin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3319","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah informed me, Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying about Ramadan: “Whoever rises during it out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.” \His sin\"""""""
"3320","Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was desiring to perform the night prayers in Ramadan without ordering them to do so. He said: “Whoever Ramadan rose out of faith and seeking reward. He will be forgiven for all his previous sins.”"
"3321","Muhammad bin Salamah reported, saying: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever observes Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, all his previous sins will be forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3322","Muhammad bin Ismail al-Tabarani told me, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Asma told us, he said: Juwayriyah told us, on the authority of Malik, he said Al-Zuhri: Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman and Humayd bin Abdul-Rahman informed me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “Whoever prays Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3323","Muhammad ibn Jabla told me, he said: Al-Mu’afā told us, he said: Musa told us, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: He informed me Urwa, that Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to encourage people to pray Ramadan without ordering them to do so. With the determination of a matter in him, he says: “Whoever observes Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ishaq Ibn Rashid is not as strong as Al-Zuhri, and Musa Ibn Ayan is trustworthy. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3324","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, he said: Abu Zumail, he is Ibn al-Walid, told us Simak al-Hanafi, on the authority of Malik ibn Marthad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about Laylat al-Qadr. Ramadan is it? He said: “Yes.” I said: “Should you be with the prophets? When they are raised up, they will be raised up until the Day of Resurrection?” He said: “Rather, until the Day of Resurrection.” Then The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated it and he narrated it, so I was confused by the neglect of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed during any Ramadan. She? He said: “In the first ten and the last ten days.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke and spoke, and the heedlessness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shaken. May God bless him and grant him peace. I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed, O Messenger of God. What are the twenty days? He said: “In the last ten days.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke. And it happened, and I was alarmed by the heedlessness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: By my father and my mother, O Messenger of God, I swear to you in my right for what You told me which of the ten days it was, and he became angry with me in a way that he had never been angry with like before. Then he said: “In the last seven days, do not ask me. \about anything after that\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"3325","Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Issa, who is the son of Al-Qasim bin Sami, he said: Humaid al-Taweel told us, On the authority of Anas ibn Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “I have been commanded to fight the polytheists until they bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, so when they testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and they perform our prayers, and face our qiblah And they ate our sacrifices, so their blood and their property were forbidden to us, except by right.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3326","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Naeem Al-Marwazi told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Humaid al-Taweel, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger God, then when they bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, and face our qiblah, and eat our sacrifice, and perform our prayer, Their blood and their property are inviolable to us except by right. They will have what the Muslims have, and they will have what they owe.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3327","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari informed us, he said: Humaid informed us, he said: Maimun ibn Siyah asked Anas bin Malik said: O Abu Hamza, the blood and property of a Muslim are not forbidden. He said: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger God, and he faced our qiblah, and performed our prayer, and ate our sacrifice, then he is a Muslim. He has the same rights as a Muslim, and he owes what a Muslim owes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3328","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Amr bin Asim told us, he said: Imran Abu Al-Awwam told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, the Arabs turned away, so Omar said: O Abu Bakr, how do you fight? Arabs? Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger.” God, and they establish prayer and pay zakat. “By God, if they had withheld from me a caretaker of what they used to give the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would have fought them for it,” he said. Omar: When I saw Abu Bakr’s opinion explained, I knew that it was the truth. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3329","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died and Abu Bakr was appointed as his successor, and those of the Arabs who disbelieved became infidels, Omar said to Abu Bakr: How do you fight people? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but God. So whoever says there is no god but God will be protected from me.” his wealth and his soul except according to his rights and his reckoning is with God.” Abu Bakr said: By God, I will fight whoever differentiates between prayer and zakat, for zakat is the right of money. By God, if they had withheld from me a camel that they were giving to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would have fought them for withholding it. Omar said: It is only because I I saw God open Abu Bakr’s heart to fight, so I knew that it was the truth."
"3330","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah Ibn Utba, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but God. So if they say it, then their blood and their property are protected from me except according to what is due therein and their reckoning is with God.” When the apostasy occurred, Omar said to Abu Bakr: Do you fight them, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say such-and-such, and he said: By God, I do not differentiate between prayer and zakat. And I will fight whoever separates them, and we will fight with him, and we see that as soundness. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3331","He said: Al-Harith bin Miskin. It was read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. He said: He told me. Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said that Abu Hurairah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been ordered to fight the people until they say: No.” There is no god but Allah, so whoever says: There is no god but Allah, his wealth and his soul will be protected from me except according to what is due to him, and his reckoning is with God Almighty,” Abu Abd said. The Most Gracious: Shuaib bin Abi Hamza collected all the two hadiths."
"3332","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Othman told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah told us Ibn Utbah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died and Abu Bakr was after him, and whoever disbelieved whoever disbelieved The Arabs, Omar said: O Abu Bakr, how do you fight the people when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god.” Except Allah, so whoever says there is no god but Allah, his wealth and his soul will be protected from me, except according to his right and his reckoning is with God Almighty.” Abu Bakr said: “I will fight those who Differentiate between prayer and zakat. Zakat is the right of money. By God, if they withheld a single hug from me, they would give it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I would have fought them for preventing it. Omar said: By God, it is not the case unless I saw God open Abu Bakr’s heart to fight, then I knew it was the truth. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3333","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Othman told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab told me, that Abu Hurairah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but God. He said it, and he protected himself and his wealth from me except according to his right and his reckoning is with God.” Al-Walid ibn Muslim disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3334","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Mu’mal bin Al-Fadl told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told me, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, and another mentioned, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Abu Bakr agreed To fight them, so Omar said: O Abu Bakr, how do you fight the people when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: No.” There is no god but God, so when they say it, their blood and their property are protected from me except by what is due to it.” Abu Bakr said: I will fight whoever differentiates between prayer and zakat, and by God, if they withhold a single female from me, they will give it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I would have fought them for preventing it. Omar said: By God, it is only because I saw that God had opened Abu Bakr’s heart to fight them, so I knew that it was the truth."
"3335","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Makhrami told us, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us. And Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but God. If they say it, their blood and their property will be withheld from me except... And their reckoning is with God Almighty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3336","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ali bin Ubaid informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, and on the authority of Abu Salih On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but God.” And when they say it They withheld from me their blood and their property except with due rights and their reckoning is with God.”"
"3337","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ziyad bin Qays, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “We fight people until they say: There is no god but God. When they say: There is no god but God “Their blood and their property are inviolable to us except by right and their reckoning is with God.”"
"3338","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man came and walked with him and said: “Kill him,” then he said: “Do you bear witness that no “There is no god but God?” He said: “Yes, but he says it as a form of refuge.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not kill him, for I have only been commanded to fight.” people until they say: There is no god but Allah, then when they say, their blood and their properties are protected from me except for what is rightful and their reckoning is with Allah,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: This hadith of Al-Aswad bin Amir is wrong, and the following is correct. Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ubaid Allah told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salem, on the authority of a man who told him, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon us while we were in the dome of the Medina Mosque, and said therein: “I have been inspired to fight people.” Until they say: There is no god but Allah,” and the like. Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Samak told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man. Bin Salem, he said: I heard Awsa saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon us while we were in a dome, and the hadith narrated (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3339","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, he said: I heard Awsa, saying: I came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with the Thaqif delegation, and I was with him in a dome, and whoever was in the dome except me and others slept, and a man came and comforted him. He said: “Go and kill him.” He said: “Does he not bear witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God?” He said: He bears witness, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he, peace and blessings be upon him, mentioned a word that means an atom, then he said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. If they say it, it is forbidden.” Their blood and their property, except for what is due to it.” Muhammad said: So I said to Shu’bah: Is it not in the hadith? Then he said: “Does he not bear witness that there is no god but God?” And I am the Messenger of God. He said: I think she is with her, but I do not know. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3340","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abdullah bin Bakr told us, he said: Hatim bin Abi Saghira told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salem, that Amr bin Aws told him that his father Aws said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been ordered to fight the people until They bear witness that there is no god but Allah, then their blood and their property will be forbidden unless it is permissible.”"
"3341","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abu Idris, he said: I heard Muawiyah, giving a sermon, but he spoke very little about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard him giving a sermon, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. God, upon him be peace, says: “All sins, perhaps God will forgive them, except for a man who kills a believer intentionally, or a man who dies as an unbeliever.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3342","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No soul is killed unjustly unless the first son of Adam owes a measure of its blood, and that is He was the first to enact killing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3343","Muhammad bin Muawiyah bin Malij informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Salama al-Harrani told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, On the authority of Ismail, the client of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, killing a believer is greater in the sight of God than the disappearance of this world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3344","Yahya bin Hakim Al-Basri told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The disappearance of this world is easier in the sight of God than the killing of a Muslim man.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3345","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: “ “Killing a believer is greater in the sight of God than the disappearance of this world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3346","Amr bin Hisham told us, he said: Mukhlid bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: “Killing a believer is greater in the sight of God than the disappearance of this world.”"
"3347","Al-Hasan bin Ishaq Al-Marwazi told us trustworthy, Khalid bin Khaddash told us, he said: Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Killing a believer is greater in the sight of God.” From the disappearance of the world.”"
"3348","Sari` bin Abdullah al-Wasiti, who was a Homsi, told us: Ishaq bin Yusuf al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The first thing for which a servant will be held accountable is prayer, and the first thing that will be made up among the people in \Blood\"""""""
"3349","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala told us, on the authority of Khaled, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abu Wa’il speaking, on the authority of Abdullah The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The first thing to be decided between people is blood.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3350","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Amir told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The first matter to be judged among the people on the Day of Resurrection will be blood.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3351","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, meaning Al-Hafari, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, he said: He said Abdullah: “The first thing that will be judged among the people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed.”"
"3352","Ahmad bin Hafs told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, then he mentioned a word. Its meaning is on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “The first thing that will be judged among the people on the Day of Resurrection will be blood.”"
"3353","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The first thing that will be judged among people on the Day of Resurrection will be blood.”"
"3354","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “The first It will be judged between people in bloodshed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3355","Ibrahim bin Al-Mustamir Basri told us, he said: Amr bin Asim told us, he said: Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salamah, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The man comes taking In the man’s hand, and he says: O Lord, this man killed me. Then God says to him: “Why did you kill him?” So he says: I killed him so that you might have glory. Then he says: It is mine.” And the man comes, taking the man’s hand, and says: This man killed me. Then God says to him: “Why did you kill him?” And he says: So that it may be The pride belongs to so-and-so, and he says, “It does not belong to so-and-so,” and he commits his sin. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3356","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juniy, He said: Jundub said: So-and-so told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The murdered person will bring his killer on the Day of Resurrection, and he will say: Ask this man why he killed me, and he will say: I killed him over the kingdom of so-and-so.” Jundub said: So beware of it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3357","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dahni, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, that Ibn Abbas was asked about who He killed a believer intentionally, then he repented and believed and did righteous deeds, then he was guided. Ibn Abbas said: How can guidance be given to him? I heard your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “He will come clinging to the killer, his veins dripping with blood, and he will say: O Lord, ask this man why he killed me?” Then he said: By God, he has indeed God sent it down and then did not abrogate it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3358","He said: Azhar bin Jamil Al-Basri told me, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, said: The people of Kufa disagreed regarding this verse, and whoever kills a believer intentionally, I went to Ibn Abbas. So I asked him, and he said: “It was revealed at the last time it was revealed, and then nothing abrogated it.”"
"3359","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas, “Does anyone who intentionally kills a believer have any repentance?” He said: No, and I read to him the verse that is in the Furqan, and those who do not They call upon another god with God, and they do not kill the soul that God has made sacred, except in truth. He said: This is a Meccan verse that was abrogated by a Medinan verse. And whoever “Whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell.”"
"3360","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said: He commanded me Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, asked Ibn Abbas about these two verses, “And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell for an eternity.” So I asked him, and he said: Nothing has abrogated it, and about this verse: And those who with God do not call upon any other god and do not kill the soul that He has forbidden. God, except with the truth. He said: It was revealed about the people of polytheism. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3361","Hajib bin Sulaiman Al-Munbiji told us, he said: Ibn Abi Rawad told us, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, on the authority of Abd al-Ala al-Thaalabi, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “Indeed, there were people who killed and increased in number, committed adultery and increased in number, and violated, so they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They said: O Muhammad, indeed what you say and to which you call is true, if you had told us that for what we had done it would be an expiation, so God Almighty and Majestic sent down And those who do not call upon any other god with God, and do not kill a soul which God has made sacred, except in a just way, and do not commit adultery - for such - God will change their evil deeds. good deeds, and God is Forgiving and Merciful. He said: God will change their polytheism into faith, and their adultery into conceit. And it was revealed: Say, O My servants who have transgressed against me. themselves the sign.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3362","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Ya’la told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, “Some polytheists came to Muhammad and said, ‘Indeed, what you say and call for is good, if only you could tell us that we would not have done it. Atonement, so it was revealed: “And those who call upon no other god with God, nor do they kill.” And it was revealed: “Say, ‘O My servants who have transgressed against themselves.’” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3363","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, he said: Warqa’ told me, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The murdered person will bring the killer on the Day of Resurrection, with his forelock and head in his hand, and his buttocks dripping with blood, saying: Oh My Lord, He killed me until He brought Him close to the Throne.” He said: Then they mentioned repentance to Ibn Abbas, so he recited this verse. And whoever kills a believer intentionally, he said: It has not been abrogated since it was revealed, and how can he repent? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3364","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Al-Ansari told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zayd, On the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, he said: “This verse was revealed, and whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell to abide therein, in which the entire verse is after The verse that was revealed in Al-Furqan “six months.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Muhammad ibn Amr did not hear it from Abu al-Zinad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3365","Muhammad bin Bashar told me, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Kharija bin Zaid, on the authority of Zaid, in his saying: “And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell to abide therein.” He said: This was revealed The verse after the one in Blessed is the Distinction is eight months. And those who do not call upon any other god with God, nor kill any soul which God has made sacred, except “In truth,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu al-Zinad entered between him and the exit of Mujalid ibn Awf. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3366","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Ibrahim, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Mujalid ibn Awf, who said: I heard Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit speaking, on the authority of his father, who said: “It was revealed: And whoever kills a believer? intentionally, so his recompense is Hell to abide therein. We feared it, so the verse was revealed that contains the Criterion: And those who call upon no other god with God, nor They kill the soul that God has forbidden except in truth.”"
"3367","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Baqiyya informed us, he said: Buhair bin Saeed narrated to me, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, that Abu Rahim Al-Sam’i narrated to them, that Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari narrated to him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever comes to worship God and does not If he associates anything with Him, establishes prayer, pays zakat, and avoids sinful sins, Paradise will belong to him.” So they asked him about the sins, and he said: “Associating By God, killing a Muslim soul, and fleeing on the day of the advance.”"
"3368","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Bakr, He said: I heard a person saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The major sins: associating others with God, disobeying one’s parents, and killing oneself. And false speech\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"3369","Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim informed me, he said: Ibn Shumail informed us, he said: Shu`bah informed us, he said: Firas informed us, he said: I heard Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The major sins: associating partners with God, and being disobedient to one’s parents.” And killing a soul, and a false oath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3370","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Muadh bin Hani told us, he said: Harb bin Shaddad told us, he said: Yahya bin Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Sinan, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Umair, that his father narrated to him and he was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: A man said: O Messenger of God, what are the major sins? He said: “There are seven of them, the greatest of which are associating others with God, killing oneself unjustly, and fleeing on the Day of March.” Mukhtasar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3371","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Amr bin Sharhabeel, on the authority of Abdullah, said: I said: O Messenger of God, which sin is greater? He said: “To make God a rival while He created you.” I said: Then what? He said: “To kill your son for fear that he might want to eat with you.” I said: Then what? He said: “To commit adultery with your neighbor’s wife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3372","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Wasil told me, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: I said: O Messenger of God, which sin is greater? He said: “To make God a rival while He created you.” I said: Then what? He said: “To kill your son in order for him to eat with you.” I said: Then what? He said: “Then you commit adultery with your neighbour’s wife.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more correct than the one before them."
"3373","Abdah bin Abdullah informed us, he said: Yazid informed us, he said: Shu’bah informed us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abd. God, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Which sin is the greatest? He said: “Shirk is to make God a rival, to commit adultery with your neighbour’s wife, and to kill your child for fear of poverty lest he eat with you.” Then Abdullah recited: And those who do not call upon another god with God, nor kill the soul that God has made sacred, except justly, and do not commit adultery. Abu Abdullah said. Al-Rahman: This is a mistake. We do not know of anyone who continued to add to it."
"3374","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdul Rahman informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One besides Whom there is no god, it is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim man who bears witness that there is no god.” There is no god but God, and I am the Messenger of God, except for three people: the one who abandons Islam and separates from the community, the married man who commits adultery, and a life for a life.” Al-Amash said: So I told him about it to Abraham, and he told me, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, something similar."
"3375","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Ghalib, he said Aisha said: Did you not know that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim man, except a man who committed adultery after being married to him. Or he disbelieves after his conversion to Islam, or a life for a life.” Zuhayr paused."
"3376","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Ghalib, he said Aisha said: O Ammar, do you not know that it is not permissible to shed a person’s blood except for three things: a life for a life, or a man who committed adultery after being married?"
"3377","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Muhammad bin Issa told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said : Abu Umamah bin Sahl and Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi’ah told me, saying: We were with Uthman while he was besieged, and when we entered We entered and prostrated, but we did not hear the words of those in the court. Then Othman entered one day and then came out, changing his complexion, and said: They are threatening to kill me. We said: May God suffice you for them. He said: Why do they kill me? I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in one of three cases: a man who disbelieved after his conversion to Islam, or who committed adultery after “By God, I have never committed adultery during pre-Islamic times or Islam, nor have I ever wished to have my religion in exchange for it since He guided me.” By God, I have not killed a soul, so why should they kill me? ! (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3378","Ahmad bin Yahya Al-Sufi told me, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Yazid bin Mardanabah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of Arfaja bin Dharih Al-Ashja’i said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the pulpit addressing the people, and he said: “There will be hardships after me.” And here are times, so whoever you see has left the group or wants to separate from the affairs of the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, whoever he may be, then kill him, for the hand of God is with the group, and Satan runs with whoever separates from the group.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3379","Abu Ali Muhammad bin Yahya told us, he said: Abdullah bin Uthman, meaning Abadan, told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah. On the authority of Arfaja bin Shuraih, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There will be humiliations and humiliations after me.” He raised his hands, so whoever you saw wanting Disperse the affairs of the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they are all together, so kill him, whoever he may be among the people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3380","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Ziyad bin Ulaqah told us, on the authority of Arfaja, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There will be tribulations and tribulations after me. So whoever wants to divide the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he is all, so strike him with the sword.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3381","Muhammad bin Qudamah Al-Masisi told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Ata bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of Usama Ibn Sharik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any man who sets out to divide my nation, strike him with the sword.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3382","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj al-Sawaf, he said: Abu Raja’, the servant of Abu Qalaba, told us He said: Abu Qalaba told us, he said: Anas bin Malik told me, that a group of eight people came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they occupied the city and their bodies became weak. They complained about this to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Don’t you go out with our shepherd in His camels, so you could drink some of their milk and urine? They said: Yes, so they went out and drank some of their milk and urine, and killed a shepherd. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they expelled the sheep. This was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he sent and they overtook them and they were brought. So he cut off their hands and feet, gouged out their eyes, and cast them out in the sun until they died. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3383","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar told me, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Anas, that a group of people came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they converted to Islam. They went to Medina, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to do so. To go to the camels of charity and drink from their urine and milk. They did so, so they killed their herdsman and drove them, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent “So they were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet, and gouged out their eyes, and did not resolve them, and left them until They died.” Then God Almighty revealed the verse: “The recompense of those who wage war against God and His Messenger is only the verse.” Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, He said: Abu Qalaba told me, on the authority of Anas, he said: Eight people from Ukal came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned something similar to His saying, “He did not defeat them,” and He said, “So they killed the shepherd.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3384","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas, He said: “A group of people came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, from ‘Ukal or ‘Urainah, and he ordered them to go to Medina, and he ordered for them food or vaccine. They drink its milk and its urine, so they killed the shepherd and led the camels, so he sent for them, brought them, and cut off their hands. “And he covered their feet and covered their eyes.” He mentioned the difference between the transmitters of praiseworthy news, on the authority of Anas bin Malik regarding it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3385","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar and others informed me, on the authority of Humaid Al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, “People from ‘Uraynah came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they invaded Medina, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent them May God bless him and grant him peace, he went to his companions, so they drank from her milk and her urine. When they recovered, they abandoned Islam and killed the shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, as a believer. They led camels, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to track them down, and they were captured, and he cut off their hands. And their feet, and their eyes, and their backs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3386","Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: Ismail informed us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: Some people came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. From Urinah, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to them: “If you went out to our city and were there and drank from its milk And her urine.” So they did so, and when they recovered, they went to the shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they killed him and returned as infidels, seeking food from the Prophet’s dung. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he sent for them, brought them, cut off their hands and feet, and gouged out their eyes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3387","Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: People from a barn came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They invaded Medina, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: “If you went out to meet us and drank of its milk.” He said: And Qatada said: “And her urine.” So they went out to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when they recovered, they disbelieved after their conversion to Islam and were killed. He was a shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as a believer. They took water from the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and set out to fight, and he sent for them. So they were taken, and he cut off their hands and feet, and gouged out their eyes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3388","Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: Aslam, meaning people from ‘Urinah, So they went to Medina, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: “If you went out to Dhud of ours and drank of its milk,” he said. Hamid: Qatada said, on the authority of Anas: “And her urine.” So they did so, and when they became healthy, they disbelieved after their conversion to Islam and killed the shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And they took shelter from the companion of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and fled, fighting, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent for He traced them, so they were taken, so he cut off their hands and feet and gouged out their eyes, and left them in the heat until they died. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3389","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Sa’id told us, he said: Qatada told us, that Anas Ibn Malik told them that people or men from Ukal or Urainah came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: O Messenger of God, “We are the people of Dara’, and not the people of the countryside, so they took shelter in the city.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to bring animals and a shepherd. He ordered them to go out there and drink from its milk and urine. When they woke up and were near Al-Harra, they disbelieved after their conversion to Islam. They killed the shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and brought sheep to water. He sent a request among them, and they were brought. He blindfolded their eyes and cut out Their hands and feet, then he left them in the free country as they were until they died.” Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abdul-A’la, something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3390","He said: Muhammad bin Nafi’ Abu Bakr al-Basri told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Qatada and Thabit told us On the authority of Anas, that a group of people from Uraynah camped in Al-Harrah, and they came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and they invaded Medina, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered them to May God bless him and grant him peace, “that they were among the camels of charity, and that they drank from their milk and their urine, then they killed the shepherd and apostatized from Islam.” They drove camels, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to follow them, and he brought them, cut off their hands and feet, and gouged out their eyes. And he threw them into Al-Harrah.” Anas said: “I saw one of them pawing the ground with his mouth due to thirst until they died.” Mention of the disagreement between Talha bin Musarrif. And Muawiyah bin Saleh Ali Yahya bin Saeed in this hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3391","Muhammad bin Wahb bin Abi Karimah Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahim told me, Zaid told me Bin Abi Unaysa, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: Bedouins from Uraynah came to the Prophet of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So they converted to Islam and invaded Medina until their colors turned yellow and their stomachs became heavy. Then the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent them. And he handed over to him a vaccine for him. “So he ordered them to drink from its milk and its urine, until they recovered and killed its herdsmen and drove the camels, so he sent The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at their request, so he brought them, cut off their hands and feet, and gouged out their eyes,” Abd al-Malik Amir said. The believers to Anas, and he was telling him: This hadith is about disbelief or sin. He said: With disbelief. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3392","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub and Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, said: Some Arabs came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they accepted Islam. Then they fell ill, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent them to a place where they could drink from its urine and milk. They stayed in it and were baptized. To the shepherd, a servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they killed him and obtained the vaccine. They claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Oh God The family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, is thirsty tonight.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent for them, and they were taken, so he cut off Their hands, feet, and the scope of their eyes, and some of them were more than others, except that Muawiyah said, meaning in this hadith: They drove to the land of Polytheism (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3393","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Khalanji told us, he said: Malik bin Sa’ir Baraa’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of"
"3394","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Wazir, who said: Abdul Aziz told us. And Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Wazir told us, he said: Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that some people raided to obtain the vaccine of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off their hands. And their feet and the size of their eyes.” And the wording is by Ibn al-Muthanna. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3395","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that a people raided to obtain the vaccine of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “So he cut off their hands and feet and gouged out their eyes.”"
"3396","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said, meaning: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Salem informed me, And Saeed bin Abdul Rahman, and another mentioned, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, that he said: “People from ‘Urinah raided On the vaccination of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so they drank it, and killed a boy of his, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to go after them. So they were taken, and he cut off their hands and feet and gouged out their eyes.” Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed me, He said: Amr ibn al-Harith told me, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Omar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the verse about warfare was revealed about them."
"3397","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Al-Layth informed me, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad. “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off those who had stolen his vaccine and covered their eyes with fire, God rebuked him for that, so God sent down God Almighty: “The recompense of those who wage war against God and His Messenger is only the entire verse.”"
"3398","Al-Fadl bin Sahl Al-Araj told us, he said: Yahya bin Ghaylan, trustworthy and trustworthy, told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Anas, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only blinded the eyes of those because they blinded the eyes of the shepherds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3399","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us of a reading from him while I was listening. He said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told me, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, “that a Jewish man killed An Ansar slave girl was given some of her jewellery, and he threw her into a pit and smashed her head with stones, so he was taken and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to be taken away. And he was safe from being stoned until he died.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3400","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muammar told me, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Anas, “A man killed an Ansar slave girl over her jewelry, then he threw her into a pit and smashed her head with stones, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered upon him and grant him peace, to be stoned until he dies.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3401","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Waqid told me, he said: he told me My father, he said: Yazid the grammarian told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: The recompense of those who wage war against God is only And His Messenger, the verse, said: “This verse was revealed regarding the polytheists, so whoever among them repents before it is controlled against him, there is no way for him, and there is no This verse is for the Muslim man. Whoever kills and spreads corruption on earth and fights against God and His Messenger and then joins the disbelievers before they are overpowered by him is not This prevents him from being subjected to the punishment he committed.”"
"3402","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, peace and blessings be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace. He encourages charity in his sermons, and forbids imitation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3403","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, he said: Abu Amer Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, On the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except by one of three characteristics.” A married adulterer will be stoned, or a man who intentionally kills a man and he will be killed, or a man who leaves Islam to wage war against God Almighty and His Messenger and he will be killed. Or he will be crucified, or he will be banished from the earth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3404","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jarir, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a servant remains, his prayer will not be accepted until he returns to his master.”"
"3405","Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Shabi, he said: Jarir was narrating, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “ If a servant remains, his prayer will not be accepted, and if he dies, he dies as an unbeliever.” And a servant of Jarir remained, so he took him and beheaded him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3406","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, he said it was Jarir. Ibn Abdullah, he said: “If the slave is returned to the land of polytheism, he has no obligation.” There is a disagreement over Abu Ishaq."
"3407","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jarir, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a servant is sent to the land of polytheism, then his blood is permissible.”"
"3408","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Qasim told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If a servant is sent to the land of polytheism, then his blood is permissible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3409","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Khaled bin Abdul Rahman told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jarir, He said: “Any slave who remains in the land of polytheism, his blood is permissible.”"
"3410","Safwan bin Amr told me, he said: Ahmad bin Khaled Al-Wahbi told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Shabi On the authority of Jarir, he said: “Any slave who remains in the land of polytheism, his blood is permissible.”"
"3411","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jarir, he said: “Which slave is more lasting than his master?” And he caught up with the enemy, and he made himself lawful.”"
"3412","Abu Al-Azhar Ahmad ibn Al-Azhar Al-Naysaburi informed us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sulaiman Al-Razi informed us, he said: Al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, on the authority of Matar al-Warraq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “It is not permissible The blood of a Muslim person, except in one of three cases: a man who commits adultery after being married to him, he must be stoned, or he kills intentionally, so he must be punished, or he commits apostasy after If he converts to Islam, he must be killed.”"
"3413","Mu'mal bin Ihab told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, On the authority of Uthman bin Affan, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except for three things: that he commit adultery.” “After he has become a Muslim, or he kills a person and he will be killed, or he disbelieves after his conversion to Islam and he will be killed.”"
"3414","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him.”"
"3415","And Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, that some people apostatized from Islam, so Ali burned them with fire. Ibn Abbas said, “If it had been me, I would not have burned them,” the Messenger of God said. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Do not torture anyone with the punishment of God.” And if it were me, I would kill them. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever changes his religion, so kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3416","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bakr told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3417","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Ismail bin Abdullah bin Zurarah told us, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, he said: he told us Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him.”"
"3418","Musa bin Abdul Rahman Al-Masruqi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3419","Al-Hussein bin Issa told us, on the authority of Abd al-Samad, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him.”"
"3420","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that Ali was brought with people from They worshiped idols, so he burned them. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only said: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3421","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Hammad bin Masada told us, he said: Qurrah bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Humayd bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Burdah. Ibn Abi Musa Al-Ash’ari, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent him to Yemen, then he sent Mu’adh ibn Jabal after that, so when He came and said: O people, I am the messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to you. So Abu Musa threw him a pillow for him to sit on, so he came. About a man who was Jewish, then he converted to Islam, then he disbelieved, so Muadh said: “I will not sit until he is killed, by the decree of God and His Messenger, three times.” So when he was killed, he sat down. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3422","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Ahmad bin Mufaddal told us, he said: Asbat told us, and he is Ibn Nasr, he said: He claimed Al-Suddi, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, said: On the day of the conquest of Mecca, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made the people safe except four. A man and two women, and he said: “Kill them even if you find them clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba. Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl and Abdullah bin Khatal, Muqais bin Sababa, and Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Al-Sarh.” As for Abdullah bin Khatal, he reached the place while he was clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba, and Saeed bin Harith raced to him, and Ammar bin Yasser preceded him. Sa'id Ammar, who was the younger of the two men, killed him. As for Muqays ibn Sababa, people overtook him in the market and killed him. As for Ikrimah, he rode. The sea was stormy, so the ship’s owners said: Be sincere, for your gods are of no use to you here. So Ikrimah said: By God, if nothing saves me from the sea except sincerity, nothing else can save me on land. I came to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, until I put my hand in his hand, and I found that he was pardoning and generous, so he came and converted to Islam, and as for Abdullah bin Saad bin Abu al-Sarh, for he hid with Uthman ibn Affan, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called the people to pledge allegiance, he brought him until He stopped it on the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, pledge allegiance to Abdullah. He raised his head and looked at him three times. He refused all of that. So he pledged allegiance to him after three days, then he went to his friends and said: “Is there not among you a sensible man who would stand up to this? When he saw me, I withheld my hand. I pledged allegiance to him and he kills him.” They said: O Messenger of God, we do not know what is in your mind. Would you please turn your eyes to us? He said: “It is not appropriate for a prophet to have traitorous eyes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3423","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Dawud informed us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There was a man from the Ansar who converted to Islam, then he apostatized and joined polytheism, then he regretted it and sent to his people, “Ask a messenger for me.” May God bless him and grant him peace. May I repent? Then his people came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: “So-and-so has regretted it, and he has commanded us to ask you whether he has repented?” Then it was revealed: “How will God guide a people who disbelieved after they believed?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3424","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, he said: he told me My father, on the authority of Yazid the grammarian, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “In Surah An-Nahl, whoever disbelieves in God after his belief, except him He was forced to say: “For them is a great punishment.” So he abrogated and made an exception from that, and said: “Then indeed your Lord is for those who emigrated after they had been tried.” Then strive hard and be patient. Indeed, after that, your Lord is Forgiving and Merciful. He is Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh, who was in charge of Egypt. He writes to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then Satan caused him to fall, and he joined the infidels. He ordered him to be killed on the day of the conquest, so Uthman sought protection for him. Ibn Affan, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, granted him protection."
"3425","Othman bin Abdullah bin Kharzaz told us, he said: Abbad bin Musa told us, he said: Ismail bin Jafar told us, he said: he told me Israel, on the authority of Uthman al-Shaham, he said: I was leading a blind man, and I came to Ikrimah and he started speaking to us. He said: Ibn Abbas, that he was blind during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had a son’s mother, by whom he had two sons, and she used to multiply. An encounter with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and insulting him. He would rebuke her, but she would not rebuke him, and he would forbid her, but she would not stop. One night, I mentioned the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I fell into it, and I could not wait until I got up to the pickaxe and put it in her stomach and leaned on it. So I killed her and she became killed. This was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gathered the people together and said: “I ask God for a man over whom I have a right who did what he did.” So he did it unless he got up.” Then the blind man came to pamper him and said: O Messenger of God, I am her companion. She was the mother of my children and she was kind and companionable to me, and I have one of her Two stars like two pearls, but she used to gossip with you a lot and insult you, so I forbade her and she would not stop, and I rebuked her and she did not rebuke. When I mentioned you yesterday, I fell in love with you, so I got up to the pickaxe and put it in her stomach, and I leaned on her until I killed her, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do they not bear witness that her blood was shed?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3426","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Anbari’s repentance, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qudamah bin Anza, on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Aslami, said: The most cruel man is Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, so I said: Should I kill him? Then he rebuked me and said: “This is not for anyone after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Mention of the disagreement over Al-A’mash in this hadith"
"3427","Muhammad bin Al-Ala Abu Kurayb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d. On the authority of Abu Barza, he said: Abu Bakr became angry with a man, so I said: Who is he, O successor of the Messenger of God? He said: Why? I said: I will behead him if you order me to do so. He said: Did you do it? He said: Yes, he said: “By God,” meaning, then he mentioned a word that meant, “The greatness of the word I said would take away his anger.” Then he said: It was not for anyone. After Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3428","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ali told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abu Barza He said: “I passed by Abu Bakr while he was angry with one of his companions, so I said: O successor of the Messenger of God, who is this whom you were angry with? He said: Why do you ask? I said: I will strike his neck. He said: By God, meaning, my words would take away the greatness of his anger. Then he said: That was not for anyone. After Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3429","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hammad, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abu Barzah, said: Abu Bakr became angry with a man, so Abu Barzah said: Should I not behead him? He said: So my statement went away with his general anger. He said: And you did it? He said, “If you had commanded me, I would have done it.” He said, “By God, this has not been the case for any human being after Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This more deserving of what is correct, and God knows best (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3430","Muawiyah bin Salih Al-Ash’ari told us, he said: Abdullah bin Jaafar told us, he said: Ubayd Allah, who is Ibn Amr, told us, on the authority of Zaid, On the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Barza, he said: “Abu Bakr became very angry with a man until his color changed. I said: O successor of the Messenger of God, by God, if you command me, I will behead him. It is as if cold water had been poured over him. Then his anger went away from the man. He said: “May your mother be bereaved of you, Abu Barzah. She was not for anyone after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: “This Incorrect and correct: Abu Nasr was contradicted by Shu`bah."
"3431","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Nasr speaking, On the authority of Abu Barza, he said: “I came to Abu Bakr, and he had treated a man harshly and he responded to him, so I said: Should I not behead him? Then he rebuked me, saying: It is not for anyone after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Nasr bin Hilal, and it was narrated on his authority by Yunus bin Ubaid, so he supported him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3432","Abu Dawud told me, he said: Affan told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal On the authority of Abdullah bin Mutarrif bin Al-Shakheer, on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Aslami, that he said: “We were with Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, and he became angry with a man from Muslims, and his anger at him became very intense. When I saw that, I said: O successor of the Messenger of God, I behead him. When I mentioned killing, he struck me. Regarding that hadith, he added something else like that, so when we separated, he sent to me and said: O Abu Barza, what did you say and I forgot what? I said, I said: Remind him, he said: Do you not remember what you said? I said: No, by God. He said: Did you see that when you saw me angry with a man, you said: Hit him. His neck, O successor of the Messenger of God, do you not remember that or were you the one who did that? I said: Yes, by God, if you command me, I will do it. He said: “By God, I will not do it.” It is for anyone after Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith is the best and finest of hadiths, and God Almighty I know (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3433","Muhammad ibn al-Ala informed us, on the authority of Ibn Idris, he said: Shu`bah informed us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, On the authority of Safwan bin Assal, he said: A Jew said to his friend: Take us to this prophet. His friend said to him: Do not say: Prophet, if only He heard you and had four eyes. They came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about nine clear signs. He said to them: “Do not associate Do not commit anything against God, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill a person which God has forbidden except in a just way, do not go with an innocent to a person in authority, and do not Prepare the pre-dawn meal, and do not consume usury, and do not slander a married woman, and do not turn away on the day of the advance, and it is incumbent upon you, especially the Jews, not to transgress on the Sabbath.” So they accepted His hands and feet, and they said: We bear witness that you are a prophet. He said: What prevents you from following me? They said: David prayed that he would not be removed from His descendants are a prophet, and we fear that if we follow you, you will kill us as Jews. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abd al-Rahman: He narrated on the authority of Shu`bah. He said: I asked Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Salamah, and he said: You recognize and you deny, Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: And Abdullah bin Salamah Al-Aftas, abandoned hadith. Abu Abd Al-Rahman said: This Al-Aftas was seeking to have hadith with Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan, and one of his teeth was (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3434","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abbad bin Maysara Al-Manqari told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever ties a knot and then blows on it has committed witchcraft, and whoever has done witchcraft has committed shirk, and whoever attaches something to And it was entrusted to him.”"
"3435","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibn Hayyan, meaning Yazid, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, who said: “The Prophet bewitched May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A Jewish man complained about this for several days. Then Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to him and said: A Jewish man bewitched you. He made a contract for you in such-and-such a well, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent for them and they extracted them, and they were brought to him and he analyzed them, so he stood up. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as if he had been loosened by a headband. He did not mention that to that Jew, nor did he ever see his face.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3436","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Sammak, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told me, he said: Khalaf bin Tamim told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, he said: Samak bin Harb told us, on the authority of Qaboos bin Mukhariq, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Sufyan Al-Thawri narrating this hadith. He said: He came A man went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: The man comes to me and wants my money. He said: “Remind him of God.” He said: What if he does not remember? He said: “Then seek the help of those around you from among the Muslims.” He said: What if there are no Muslims around me? He said: “Then seek the help of the Sultan against him.” He said: What if the Sultan turns away from me? He said: “Fight without your money until you are among the martyrs of the Hereafter or withhold your money.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3437","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Amr bin Quhayd al-Ghifari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, what do you think if my property is attacked? He said: “Then seek refuge in God.” He said: So if they refuse me? He said: “Then seek refuge in God.” He said: So if they refuse me? He said: “Then seek refuge in God.” He said: So if they refuse me? He said: “Then fight, and if you are killed, then in Paradise, and if you are killed, then in Hell.”"
"3438","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Layth, who said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Haad, on the authority of Quhaid bin Mutrif al-Ghifari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, have you seen? What if my money is violated? He said: “Then seek refuge in God.” He said: So if they refuse me? He said: “Then seek refuge in God.” He said: So if they refuse me? He said: “Then seek refuge in God.” He said: So if they refuse me? He said: “Then fight, and if you are killed, then in Paradise, and if you are killed, then in Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3439","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Hatem told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever fights for his money and is killed is a martyr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3440","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, saying: Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Abu Yunus Al-Qushayri, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Safwan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever fights for his wealth Then he was killed and is a martyr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3441","Ubayd Allah ibn Fadhalah ibn Ibrahim al-Naysaburi told me, he said: Abdullah, who is the son of Yazid al-Muqri, informed us, he said: He told us Saeed, he said: Abu Al-Aswad Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman informed us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever is killed while preserving his property unjustly, Paradise will be for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3442","Ja'far bin Muhammad bin Al-Hudhayl told us, he said: Asim bin Yusuf told us, he said: Sa'ir bin Al-Khams told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hasan On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is killed while protecting his wealth is a martyr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3443","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya, who is Ibn Saeed, told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Hassan told me, He said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Talha told me that he heard Abdullah bin Amr speaking, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Who His money was taken from him unjustly, so he fought and was killed, so he is a martyr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3444","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Talha, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is killed without his wealth is A martyr.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake and the one before it is correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3445","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim and Qutaybah informed us, and the wording is for Ishaq. He said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Talha ibn Abd. Allah bin Awf, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever is killed while protecting his property is a martyr,” brief. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3446","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abdah informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Talha ibn Abdullah bin Awf, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fights for his money is a martyr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3447","Ahmad ibn Nasr told us, he said: Al-Mu’mal told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is killed while defending his wealth is a martyr.”"
"3448","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever is killed without being unjust to him is a martyr.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of al-Mu’amil is wrong, but the correct one is Hadith of Abdul Rahman (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3449","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Ubaidah bin Muhammad, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fights Whoever protects his wealth and is killed is a martyr, and whoever fights for his blood is a martyr, and whoever fights for his family is a martyr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3450","Muhammad bin Rafi’ and Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Sulayman told us, meaning Ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, he said: Tell us Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Muhammad bin Ammar bin Yasser, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is killed while defending his property is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his family is a martyr.” And whoever is killed in defense of his religion is a martyr, and whoever is killed in defense of his religion is a martyr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3451","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Saeed bin Amr Al-Ash’athi told us, he said: Abathar told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Sawada Ibn Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: I was sitting with Suwayd ibn Muqrin, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever was killed Regardless of his injustice, he is a martyr.”"
"3452","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever draws his sword and then puts it down, his blood will be wasted.” Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us of this chain of transmission like it, but he did not transmit it."
"3453","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: “ “Whoever raises a weapon and then puts it down, his blood will be shed.”"
"3454","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Malik, Abdullah ibn Umar, and Usama informed me. Ibn Zayd, and Yunus Ibn Yazid, that Nafi’ told them, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever carries We have the weapons, but he is not of us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3455","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Al-Thawri informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of my father Saeed Al-Khudri said: Ali sent to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Yemen, some gold in its soil, and he divided it among Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis Al-Hanathili, then one of the Banu Majashi, and between Uyaynah bin Badr Al-Fazari, and between Alqamah bin Ulatha Al-Amiri, then one of the Banu Kilab And Zayd showed the Tayi horses, and then one of the Banu Nabhan, and he said: Then the Quraysh and the Ansar became angry, and they said: You will give the baskets of the people of Najd. And he left us, and he said: “I am only acquainted with them.” Then a man with sunken eyes, prominent cheeks, a thick beard, and a shaved head came and said: Oh Muhammad, fear God, said: “Who obeys God if I disobey Him? Should he trust me with the people of the earth and you do not trust me?” So he asked a man from the people who killed him. So he prevented him, and when he left, he said: “Indeed, from this poor people will come out, reciting the Qur’an, but it will not go beyond their throats, and they will be devoid of religion, devoid of religion.” \The arrow is from the target. They kill the people of Islam and call upon the people of idols. If I overtake them"
"3456","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla. On the authority of Ali, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A people will emerge at the end of time who are ignorant of their teeth and foolish dreams. They speak the best speech of the people, their faith does not go beyond their throats, they escape from religion as an arrow escapes from its target, so when you meet them So kill them, for killing them will reward those who killed them on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3457","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Basri Al-Bahrani told us, he said: Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Al-Azraq bin Qays. On the authority of Sharik bin Shihab, he said: I was hoping to meet a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to ask him about the Kharijites, but I met On the day of Eid, Abu Barza was with a group of his friends, so I said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention the Kharijites? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with my ears and I saw it with my eyes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with money and he divided it. So he gave to those on his right and to those on his left, but he did not give anything to those behind him. Then a man stood up behind him and said: O Muhammad, you have not done justice to me. Al-Qasma, a black man with combed hair and two white clothes over him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became very angry and said: By God, you will not find after me a man more just than me.” Then he said: “At the end of time, a people will emerge as if this is one of them, reciting the Qur’an without It will go beyond their throats, they will leave Islam as an arrow leaves a target, their marks will take flight. They will continue to leave until the last of them comes out with... The Antichrist, so if you meet them, kill them. They are the evil of creation and creation.” Abu Abd al-Rahman, may God have mercy on him, said: Sharik bin A shooting star is not that famous (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3458","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Omar bin Saad, he said Saad bin Abi Waqqas told us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Killing a Muslim is blasphemy and insulting him is immorality.”"
"3459","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Insulting a Muslim is immorality, and fighting him is disbelief.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3460","Yahya bin Hakim told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Insulting a Muslim is immorality, and fighting him is blasphemy.” Aban said to him: O Abu Ishaq, did you not hear it except from my father? Al-Ahwas? He said: Rather, I heard it from Al-Aswad and Hubayra."
"3461","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ra’, on the authority of his uncle Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Insulting a Muslim is immorality, and fighting him is blasphemy.”"
"3462","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: my father told us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik bin Umair talking to him, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Cursing a Muslim is immoral, and fighting him \unbelief\"""""""
"3463","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Zubaid, he said: I told Abu Wael, I heard Abdullah, saying On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Fighting a Muslim is blasphemy, and cursing at him is immorality?” He said: Yes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3464","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Insulting a Muslim is immorality and fighting him is blasphemy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3465","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: I said to Hammad: I heard Mansour and Suleiman, And Zubayd narrates, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Cursing a Muslim is immoral. And fighting him is blasphemy.” Who do you accuse? Are you accusing Mansour? Are you accusing Zubayd? Did you accuse Solomon? He said: No, but I accuse Abu Wael."
